    "providerAndPricingTierEvidence": {
      "status": "gateway_first_route_not_release_executable_for_proposed_model_policy",
      "reason": "A 2026-10-06 names-only inventory of the live SyncAI project shows LLM_BASE_URL, LLM_API_KEY, and OPENAI_API_KEY configured, with neither LLM_GATEWAY_MODEL nor DEVELOP_AGENT_MODEL present. The shipped defaults therefore reserve against gpt-4o-mini but send stigg/fast to the gateway. The shared provider chain leads with stigg-gateway and falls back to direct OpenAI. The gateway repository maps the default stigg/fast request to a Claude primary and Claude, GPT, and Gemini fallbacks, while the proposed policy allows only three canonical GPT models. SyncAI settles the provider-returned concrete model and refuses fuzzy alias pricing, so an unpriced or unapproved gateway result is recorded as a policy violation and freezes later commercial-period spend. The exact deployed gateway revision, returned model identity, CAD-normalized price schedule, fixed infrastructure allocation, and approved provider multiplier are not evidenced. A production multiplier of 1.0 and the proposed model policy are not release-eligible. No secret value was inspected."
    },
